---
layout: default
---
{% assign cv_feature_enabled = site.al_folio.features.cv.enabled | default: true %}

{% if site.plugins contains 'al_folio_cv' and cv_feature_enabled %}
  {% comment %}
    The CV markup — including its <header> — is generated by the al_folio_cv gem's
    `cv/render.liquid` template (389 lines), so there is no layout seam to insert
    into. Rather than freeze that whole template as a local override, capture the
    tag's output and splice the resume link in just before the header closes.

    The link deliberately does NOT go in `page.description`: that field feeds the
    <meta name="description"> tag, and raw HTML there would leak markup into the
    page's search-engine snippet.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% capture cv_html %}{% al_folio_cv_render %}{% endcapture %}

  {% comment %}
    Obfuscate the address in the General Information table to match the home page.
    Done here rather than in _data/cv.yml because that file is also the input to
    RenderCV, which validates `email` as a real address — writing the spelled-out
    form there would fail the render-cv workflow. Derived from the data file so the
    address is never duplicated.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% assign raw_email = site.data.cv.cv.email %}
  {% if raw_email and raw_email != '' %}
    {% assign shown_email = raw_email | replace: '@', ' (at) ' | replace: '.', ' (dot) ' %}
    {% assign cv_html = cv_html | replace: raw_email, shown_email %}
  {% endif %}

  {% comment %}
    Append the resume link inside the existing description paragraph rather than
    adding a second <p>, so the sentence and the link share one line.
  {% endcomment %}
  {% if page.resume_pdf and page.description %}
    {% capture resume_href %}{% if page.resume_pdf contains '://' %}{{ page.resume_pdf }}{% else %}{{ page.resume_pdf | relative_url }}{% endif %}{% endcapture %}
    {% capture desc_before %}{{ page.description }}</p>{% endcapture %}
    {% capture desc_after %}{{ page.description }} <a class="cv-resume-link" href="{{ resume_href | strip }}" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">You can access my resume here.</a></p>{% endcapture %}
    {% assign cv_html = cv_html | replace_first: desc_before, desc_after %}
  {% endif %}

  {{ cv_html }}
{% else %}
  <div class="post">
    <header class="post-header">
      <h1 class="post-title">{{ page.title }}</h1>
      <p class="post-description">CV rendering is unavailable.</p>
    </header>
    <article>
      <p>Enable the <code>al_folio_cv</code> plugin and set <code>al_folio.features.cv.enabled: true</code> to render this page.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
{% endif %}
